 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's annoying, and it usually the chain getting hungry for lube. Pop it between the biggest ring and the inner pin first, then give it a good tug. It works wonders, and it safe on your gear too. Pop a little on a paper bag first though, it' strong. Find the chain through the big hole each end. Drizzle on the side facing up, give it a goes, then give each pin a quick tap with pin tool. Cleanness doesn't matter, but I' like to see it bright and glossy after lube. For maintenance yes, if it looks dull it's worn and time for new chain anyway.",
